From 8b5a447d6a042fb91d3ace69bbffaa74cb39b41e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:51:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: vop2: Mask POST_BUF_EMPTY until the next flush

For as long as a video port underflows, the POST_BUF_EMPTY status is
raised again as soon as vop2_isr() clears it. On RK3568 driving
3840x2160@60, enabling a 4K AFBC cluster window on a running video port
makes the handler run about 165000 times per second, more often than
the mode has lines, until the next frame is committed, which can take
more than a second. Each of the rate-limited error messages also costs
about 0.7 ms on the serial console in hard interrupt context.

Disable the interrupt when it fires and enable it again, with its
status cleared, in vop2_crtc_atomic_flush() once the next configuration
is committed. An underflow is then reported once per committed
configuration.

Fixes: 604be85547ce ("drm/rockchip: Add VOP2 driver")
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c
@@ -1862,6 +1862,8 @@ static void vop2_crtc_atomic_flush(struc
 
 	vop2_cfg_done(vp);
 
+	vop2_crtc_enable_irq(vp, VP_INT_POST_BUF_EMPTY);
+
 	spin_lock_irq(&crtc->dev->event_lock);
 
 	if (crtc->state->event) {
@@ -2249,6 +2251,7 @@ static irqreturn_t vop2_isr(int irq, voi
 			}
 
 			if (irqs & VP_INT_POST_BUF_EMPTY) {
+				vop2_crtc_disable_irq(vp, VP_INT_POST_BUF_EMPTY);
 				drm_err_ratelimited(vop2->drm,
 						    "POST_BUF_EMPTY irq err at vp%d\n",
 						    vp->id);
